# Sound assets

**Playable sounds are already included** in this folder (`bray`, `fart`, `burp`,
`oink`, `splat`, `shake`, `chitter`, `pounce`), so the donkey brays and farts on
first run with nothing to set up. They are synthesized cartoon placeholders —
generic and swappable.

To replace any of them with your own, just drop a file with the SAME name into
this folder (any of `.wav`, `.m4a`, `.caf`, `.aiff`, `.mp3`) and rebuild. The
synchronized project folder picks it up automatically.

Which animal uses which (see `AnimalMaskConfig`):

- Donkey (gross-loud): `bray`, `fart`, `burp` — fired on mouth-open, random each time
- Pig (gross-messy): `oink`, `splat`, `shake`
- Raccoon (sneaky): `chitter`, `pounce`

If a named file is ever missing, the app falls back to a system sound so the loop
never breaks.
